180
00:08:31.270 --> 00:08:35.650
And here's something I learned when I was deep diving paper airplanes is that these paper

181
00:08:35.650 --> 00:08:41.570
airplane people who try to break these records, they tend to work in groups of three.

182
00:08:41.990 --> 00:08:48.030
So there's someone who designs the plane, someone who folds it, and then someone who throws

183
00:08:48.030 --> 00:08:48.430
it.

184
00:08:48.570 --> 00:08:50.790
And all three people get the record.

185
00:08:51.590 --> 00:08:51.830
Wow.

186
00:08:52.110 --> 00:08:58.070
These guys spent more than 400 hours over a six-month period perfecting their designs.

187
00:08:59.010 --> 00:09:04.770
It took 20 minutes to fold the design, and they used a single sheet of paper.

188
00:09:05.350 --> 00:09:06.730
In fact, there's rules.

189
00:09:07.110 --> 00:09:08.770
I was going to say, is there a rule?

190
00:09:08.910 --> 00:09:10.570
Is it like you can only have one piece of paper?

191
00:09:10.750 --> 00:09:12.890
You can't have add-ons?

192
00:09:13.050 --> 00:09:13.750
Like, what are the rules?

193
00:09:14.070 --> 00:09:14.610
That's right.

194
00:09:14.790 --> 00:09:22.850
The maximum size paper allowed is A4, and the maximum paper density is 100 grams slash M squared.

195
00:09:23.530 --> 00:09:24.590
Here's the thing.

196
00:09:24.770 --> 00:09:26.030
There's more rules.

197
00:09:26.430 --> 00:09:26.870
Oh.

198
00:09:27.190 --> 00:09:29.190
You cannot use any glue.

199
00:09:29.870 --> 00:09:31.450
You cannot cut the paper.

200
00:09:31.670 --> 00:09:33.110
You cannot tear the paper.

201
00:09:33.410 --> 00:09:34.390
Kevin, you're out.

202
00:09:34.490 --> 00:09:35.290
You're out, Kevin.

203
00:09:35.610 --> 00:09:36.010
I know.

204
00:09:36.570 --> 00:09:41.310
However, you can use one small piece of clear tape.

205
00:09:41.630 --> 00:09:45.450
It can be 25 millimeters by 30 millimeters.

206
00:09:46.410 --> 00:09:46.930
Interesting.

207
00:09:47.350 --> 00:09:52.250
Also, in order to count for the record, you have to throw the plane indoors behind a starting line.

208
00:09:52.410 --> 00:09:55.550
So you can't have any extra wind in your sails.

209
00:09:55.810 --> 00:09:56.230
Exactly.

210
00:09:56.750 --> 00:09:59.530
If your foot crosses the line, you will be disqualified.

211
00:09:59.990 --> 00:10:06.090
