01:13:09.500 --> 01:13:10.260
That's right.

1489
01:13:10.440 --> 01:13:11.920
That was like 21 seconds.

1490
01:13:12.560 --> 01:13:12.900
Mm-hmm.

1491
01:13:13.080 --> 01:13:13.920
It's longer.

1492
01:13:14.160 --> 01:13:18.240
It's the longest airplane flew longer than Jim and Pam's moment of silence.

1493
01:13:18.500 --> 01:13:18.700
Mm-hmm.

1494
01:13:20.080 --> 01:13:22.480
Oh, I hope we didn't ruin that scene for people.

1495
01:13:22.480 --> 01:13:27.540
Now, when they go back to watch that, they're going to imagine a paper airplane flying through

1496
01:13:27.540 --> 01:13:28.040
the air.

1497
01:13:28.460 --> 01:13:28.960
Sorry.

1498
01:13:30.900 --> 01:13:31.760
Here's the thing.

1499
01:13:31.900 --> 01:13:36.660
With Jenna and I doing this rewatch and watching these episodes so many times, it's the office

1500
01:13:36.660 --> 01:13:38.580
just lives in us now.

1501
01:13:38.920 --> 01:13:40.180
It lives in my brain.

1502
01:13:40.640 --> 01:13:42.580
We relate everything back to like an episode.

1503
01:13:42.580 --> 01:13:44.920
We were probably so annoying to be around.

1504
01:13:44.920 --> 01:13:49.380
Well, it's Toby's turn now, and he's just already defeated.

1505
01:13:49.600 --> 01:13:53.500
He just crumples it up, and he bails, basically.

1506
01:13:53.800 --> 01:13:54.840
So Angela wins.

1507
01:13:55.060 --> 01:13:56.060
Dwight applauds.

1508
01:13:56.300 --> 01:13:57.560
He's very happy.

1509
01:13:57.780 --> 01:13:59.400
And Esther clocks this.

1510
01:13:59.700 --> 01:14:02.940
She says, why are we happy for that little woman?

1511
01:14:03.660 --> 01:14:09.320
And then Dwight says, you know, I pity her because she could have had everything, and she lost

1512
01:14:09.320 --> 01:14:09.800
it all.

1513
01:14:10.500 --> 01:14:10.780
Yeah.

1514
01:14:11.180 --> 01:14:15.920
And now we're going to see Dwight face off against Erin, and guess who wins?

1515
01:14:17.140 --> 01:14:17.700
Dwight!

1516
01:14:18.720 --> 01:14:20.640
Ellie Kemper's reaction to losing.

1517
01:14:21.720 --> 01:14:28.860
I had to watch this scene over and over and over when she kicks that box, and her foot

1518
01:14:28.860 --> 01:14:32.540
gets stuck, and then she loses her shoe in all the popcorn.

1519
01:14:32.960 --> 01:14:33.520
Yes.

1520
01:14:33.840 --> 01:14:35.460
It was so funny.

1521
01:14:35.720 --> 01:14:37.540
And she's just like, I'm just really mad right now.

1522
01:14:37.540 --> 01:14:38.900
I'm just really mad right now.

1523
01:14:39.200 --> 01:14:40.140
I'm angry.

1524
01:14:40.580 --> 01:14:43.320
And like, clearly, that wasn't supposed to happen.

1525
01:14:43.580 --> 01:14:46.120
I don't think her foot was meant to break that box.

1526
01:14:46.280 --> 01:14:48.140
I don't think she was meant to lose her shoe.

1527
01:14:48.300 --> 01:14:50.720
And the two of them hold it together so well.

1528
01:14:50.900 --> 01:14:51.840
It's beautiful.

1529
01:14:52.140 --> 01:14:53.120
It is.

1530
01:14:53.260 --> 01:14:58.240
And I just loved what Warren and Halstead shared with us about how important this story

1531
01:14:58.240 --> 01:15:03.900
is for the Erin and Pete relationship that Pete is now starting to question it.

1532
01:15:03.900 --> 01:15:07.380
He's like, maybe we're not the right fit.

1533
01:15:08.020 --> 01:15:13.780
Well, they said they were starting to think that Pete and Erin would not end up together.

1534
01:15:13.960 --> 01:15:14.320
Yes.

1535
01:15:14.700 --> 01:15:18.600
And so they had to show a way that maybe they weren't compatible.

1536
01:15:18.900 --> 01:15:19.480
That's right.

1537
01:15:20.180 --> 01:15:24.000
Well, now we're back at Jim and Pam and Clark's desk clump.

1538
01:15:24.260 --> 01:15:28.500
And Jim and Pam are continuing to speak in their therapy speak.

1539
01:15:28.500 --> 01:15:31.620
And it's becoming more passive aggressive.

1540
01:15:32.240 --> 01:15:35.480
And Clark is like, hey, are you guys high?

1541
01:15:35.600 --> 01:15:38.180
Because if you're high, can you pass me some?

1542
01:15:38.480 --> 01:15:40.660
And they're like, no, we're not high.

1543
01:15:41.520 --> 01:15:41.680
Yeah.

1544
01:15:41.840 --> 01:15:45.040
This is when Pam is going to have her talking head where she says,

1545
01:15:45.220 --> 01:15:51.520
I just wish we'd started this exercise six months ago because my heart feels just blocked

1546
01:15:51.520 --> 01:15:52.320
up right now.

1547
01:15:52.920 --> 01:15:53.220
Yeah.

1548
01:15:53.220 --> 01:15:56.040
I felt that when she said it.

1549
01:15:56.120 --> 01:15:56.700
I felt it.

1550
01:15:56.980 --> 01:15:57.960
I did too.

1551
01:15:58.520 --> 01:16:01.620
I want you to know that there was more to this talking head.

1552
01:16:02.080 --> 01:16:07.960
She would have gone on to say, I want to believe talking like robots will help.

1553
01:16:08.080 --> 01:16:11.820
Although robots aren't really known for their emotional connections.

1554
01:16:12.480 --> 01:16:14.460
And are you ready for this, Angela?

1555
01:16:14.880 --> 01:16:16.480
No, I'm not.

1556
01:16:16.860 --> 01:16:18.940
This is what Pam would have said next.

1557
01:16:19.960 --> 01:16:24.160
Well, I guess R2-D2 and C-3PO were pretty attached.

1558
01:16:24.980 --> 01:16:26.480
Is that where we're headed?

1559
01:16:27.240 --> 01:16:29.840
She would have made a Star Wars reference.

1560
01:16:30.320 --> 01:16:30.500
Star Wars.

1561
01:16:30.700 --> 01:16:33.540
Star Wars and Lord of the Rings in one episode.

1562
01:16:33.580 --> 01:16:34.540
Come on.

1563
01:16:34.860 --> 01:16:35.480
I know.

1564
01:16:35.540 --> 01:16:41.540
It looks like Pam and Angela could be bonding over their love of sci-fi filMs.

1565
01:16:42.420 --> 01:16:44.120
That's a scene I want to see.

1566
01:16:44.340 --> 01:16:47.900
I want to see the two of them in the break room talking sci-fi.

1567
01:16:47.900 --> 01:16:48.920
Mm-hmm.

1568
01:16:49.640 --> 01:16:52.340
Kevin is still working really hard on paper airplanes.

1569
01:16:52.520 --> 01:16:55.140
There is a whole table of airplanes.

1570
01:16:55.340 --> 01:16:56.780
And now he's gluing stuff.

1571
01:16:56.780 --> 01:16:58.380
He's pasting things together.

1572
01:16:58.680 --> 01:17:00.120
It's such a mess.

1573
01:17:00.260 --> 01:17:02.120
This is like crafting gone wrong.

1574
01:17:02.680 --> 01:17:07.240
This scene is completely unnecessary for the plot of this episode.

1575
01:17:07.240 --> 01:17:09.920
But it is an absolute delight.

1576
01:17:10.080 --> 01:17:16.620
It is a display of beautiful comic timing, both physical and oral.

1577
01:17:16.620 --> 01:17:18.340
Is that a type of comedy?

1578
01:17:18.640 --> 01:17:19.340
Oral comedy?

1579
01:17:19.560 --> 01:17:20.340
I guess it is.

1580
01:17:20.840 --> 01:17:23.180
Anyway, all of his timing is beautiful.

1581
01:17:23.200 --> 01:17:25.040
I really enjoyed this moment.

1582
01:17:25.720 --> 01:17:28.120
It's now time for the final round.

1583
01:17:28.520 --> 01:17:30.260
It is Angela versus Dwight.

1584
01:17:30.820 --> 01:17:33.040
Dwight had a talking head that was deleted.

1585
01:17:33.040 --> 01:17:37.300
And he talks about why he doesn't need the money, but Angela does.

1586
01:17:37.480 --> 01:17:38.540
And I thought you should hear it.

1587
01:17:39.400 --> 01:17:40.520
I don't need this win.

1588
01:17:40.700 --> 01:17:43.660
I've got a lucrative job, an enormous farm, and this building.

1589
01:17:44.160 --> 01:17:50.420
Angela has nothing but a child who, while adorable, won't bring in revenue for another five or six years.

1590
01:17:51.600 --> 01:17:52.860
That's so interesting.

1591
01:17:53.780 --> 01:17:58.380
It's very shrewd, isn't it, that he thinks Philip is going to be working in five years?

1592
01:18:00.340 --> 01:18:03.040
It is, but he's, you know, yeah.

1593
01:18:03.260 --> 01:18:06.580
He has an interesting way of attaching value to things.

1594
01:18:06.920 --> 01:18:09.440
Well, Angela's first throw is terrible.

1595
01:18:10.040 --> 01:18:12.940
And then Dwight fumbles his on purpose.

1596
01:18:13.940 --> 01:18:14.920
Esther clocks this.

1597
01:18:15.120 --> 01:18:19.760
It's said in the script, Esther sees Dwight do this and is jealous.

1598
01:18:21.460 --> 01:18:23.600
Yes, that's what it said in the shooting draft.

1599
01:18:23.900 --> 01:18:29.740
And then she goes over to Angela and she's very patronizing and says, you know, they want her to win.

1600
01:18:29.920 --> 01:18:32.700
They know she needs this money, so use it wisely.

1601
01:18:33.000 --> 01:18:36.780
And then Esther strokes sort of the back of Angela's hair.

1602
01:18:37.040 --> 01:18:38.340
That was not scripted.

1603
01:18:38.540 --> 01:18:39.780
Nora improvised that.

1604
01:18:39.980 --> 01:18:46.660
And then I reacted and improvised as Angela would react, which is horrified that this woman has touched her hair.

1605
01:18:46.880 --> 01:18:48.200
It was so fun.

1606
01:18:48.200 --> 01:18:51.320
And when Nora did it, we were like, okay, you've got to keep doing that.

1607
01:18:51.560 --> 01:18:55.880
And then Angela goes over to Dwight and she says, do not tank this.

1608
01:18:56.100 --> 01:18:57.700
Like, she doesn't want his pity.

1609
01:18:58.160 --> 01:19:01.760
Well, at first she's very delighted by the gesture.

1610
01:19:01.760 --> 01:19:06.320
But when Esther gets involved, she's like, no, her pride comes out.

1611
01:19:06.520 --> 01:19:07.080
That's right.

1612
01:19:07.580 --> 01:19:11.280
Angela is going to go up to Dwight now and says, do not tank this throw.

1613
01:19:11.760 --> 01:19:14.120
And so he throws and it goes far.

1614
01:19:14.340 --> 01:19:16.640
And then she purposely tanks hers.

1615
01:19:17.700 --> 01:19:19.140
I loved this moment.

1616
01:19:19.520 --> 01:19:25.760
Because Nora had improvised touching the back of my hair, we knew I had to touch her head somehow.

1617
01:19:26.020 --> 01:19:26.480
Yeah.

1618
01:19:26.580 --> 01:19:28.260
But she's so much taller than me.

1619
01:19:28.680 --> 01:19:32.520
So Angela goes up to Esther and says, I guess you guys needed the money more than me.

1620
01:19:32.780 --> 01:19:34.080
And then I improvise.

1621
01:19:34.240 --> 01:19:34.560
Huh.

1622
01:19:34.980 --> 01:19:36.020
Use it wisely.

1623
01:19:36.020 --> 01:19:38.620
And I touched her forehead and hair.

1624
01:19:39.160 --> 01:19:41.640
And I saunter off very pridefully.

1625
01:19:42.200 --> 01:19:46.240
So that was a really fun back and forth that I got to have with Nora.

1626
01:19:46.460 --> 01:19:47.700
I love that she did that.

1627
01:19:47.800 --> 01:19:49.580
And then I love that I got to have that response.

1628
01:19:50.480 --> 01:19:51.900
Well, I loved this whole moment.

1629
01:19:52.060 --> 01:19:53.620
I really didn't know what was going to happen.

1630
01:19:53.860 --> 01:19:58.440
I didn't know if Dwight was going to find a way to let Angela win.

1631
01:19:58.440 --> 01:20:01.520
But all of it was just so in character for you guys.

1632
01:20:01.520 --> 01:20:03.440
And I think that's what I liked about it.

1633
01:20:03.680 --> 01:20:06.740
I also love Angela's talking head when she's like, you know what?

1634
01:20:06.840 --> 01:20:08.260
Dwight showed weakness today.

1635
01:20:08.580 --> 01:20:09.860
And I don't need it.

1636
01:20:09.900 --> 01:20:10.800
I don't need his pity.

1637
01:20:11.040 --> 01:20:12.380
I have my dignity.

1638
01:20:12.380 --> 01:20:16.080
And as she's saying it, she's stealing all the toilet paper from the bathroom.

1639
01:20:16.580 --> 01:20:17.060
Mm-hmm.

1640
01:20:17.320 --> 01:20:22.020
It did say in the script that even as she walks out with all that toilet paper, she's holding her head high.

1641
01:20:22.740 --> 01:20:24.200
Yes, I read that too.

1642
01:20:24.200 --> 01:20:27.600
Well, that's the end of our paper airplane storyline.

1643
01:20:27.600 --> 01:20:39.360
And just to wrap things up, I thought y'all might like to know that the largest flying paper airplane is a 53-pound paper glider that flew 59 feet.

1644
01:20:39.800 --> 01:20:43.980
It has a wingspan of 60 feet, a length of 17 feet.

1645
01:20:44.280 --> 01:20:51.180
And it was constructed in Germany in 2013 by a team of 16 university students and employees.

1646
01:20:51.880 --> 01:20:59.540
A larger paper airplane was built in Fitchburg, USA in 2018, but it was not able to fly.

1647
01:21:00.080 --> 01:21:00.600
Ah.

1648
01:21:01.360 --> 01:21:02.000
Yes.

1649
01:21:02.260 --> 01:21:07.640
And that concludes your paper airplane tidbits.

1650
01:21:07.940 --> 01:21:09.000
I love them.

1651
01:21:09.240 --> 01:21:10.400
Thank you very much.

1652
01:21:10.640 --> 01:21:14.640
The next scene made me tear up and I was not expecting it.

1653
01:21:14.640 --> 01:21:16.840
But I was sort of surprised.

1654
01:21:17.000 --> 01:21:19.100
I hadn't seen this episode since it aired.

1655
01:21:20.720 --> 01:21:24.280
And this whole Jim and Pam ending really got me, lady.

1656
01:21:25.140 --> 01:21:28.540
You know, Jim is going to tell Pam that he's sorry that he has to go.

1657
01:21:28.780 --> 01:21:30.260
It's time for him to go back to Philly.

1658
01:21:30.680 --> 01:21:34.120
But he thinks they should keep working at this because they're making progress.

1659
01:21:34.680 --> 01:21:37.940
And he kind of does that thing where he looks back, but she doesn't.

1660
01:21:38.000 --> 01:21:41.480
And then he leaves and then she looks towards the door, but he's already left.

1661
01:21:41.760 --> 01:21:49.260
And then she sees that he left his umbrella and she hesitates for a second and decides to try to catch him to give it to him.

1662
01:21:49.980 --> 01:21:57.360
Well, that scene at the desk where Jim comes really close to Pam, I remember when we were shooting this,

1663
01:21:57.480 --> 01:22:04.180
that this is the first time that our characters had been in one another's intimate personal space in a really long time.

1664
01:22:04.500 --> 01:22:04.740
Yeah.

1665
01:22:04.960 --> 01:22:11.160
And not only was he in her sort of close proximity, but he was gentle.

1666
01:22:11.440 --> 01:22:12.380
He kneeled down.

1667
01:22:12.580 --> 01:22:13.520
He was next to her.

1668
01:22:13.660 --> 01:22:14.680
He was being earneSt.

1669
01:22:14.680 --> 01:22:20.680
There was a connection between the two of them in that moment that we haven't seen in many episodes.

1670
01:22:20.960 --> 01:22:22.500
He was being Jim.

1671
01:22:22.880 --> 01:22:23.200
Yeah.

1672
01:22:23.380 --> 01:22:24.800
He was being old Jim.

1673
01:22:25.060 --> 01:22:27.480
All of the posturing of athlete was gone.

1674
01:22:27.700 --> 01:22:32.040
And he was being the guy that she fell in love with.

1675
01:22:32.220 --> 01:22:32.720
That's right.

1676
01:22:32.920 --> 01:22:34.880
And it was very moving to me.

1677
01:22:35.060 --> 01:22:43.740
And it was hard for me to not kind of melt in that moment as Pam, you know, because she's wanted this for a really long time.

1678
01:22:43.740 --> 01:22:46.680
So this was a really fun scene to play.

1679
01:22:46.900 --> 01:22:48.080
It had a lot of levels.

1680
01:22:48.500 --> 01:22:51.440
And then it leads to the scene in the parking lot.

1681
01:22:51.660 --> 01:22:54.560
Pam decides to run out and give Jim his umbrella.

1682
01:22:54.860 --> 01:22:56.520
And he hugs her.

1683
01:22:56.740 --> 01:22:58.360
And I wrote this to you, Jenna.

1684
01:22:58.480 --> 01:22:59.440
We were trading texts.

1685
01:22:59.660 --> 01:23:04.400
I said, Jim hugs Pam like she's the last life preserver on the Titanic.

1686
01:23:04.700 --> 01:23:05.400
I know.

1687
01:23:05.400 --> 01:23:07.020
He grabbed onto her.

1688
01:23:07.220 --> 01:23:08.000
He does.

1689
01:23:08.140 --> 01:23:10.500
And this is just such a beautiful scene.

1690
01:23:10.500 --> 01:23:12.260
Pam is resistant at firSt.

1691
01:23:12.380 --> 01:23:17.460
And he just will not let her go until she breaks down that wall.

1692
01:23:17.460 --> 01:23:18.940
And she hugs him back.

1693
01:23:19.060 --> 01:23:20.120
And they kiss.

1694
01:23:20.260 --> 01:23:21.460
And they say, I love you.

1695
01:23:21.680 --> 01:23:22.600
I teared up.

1696
01:23:22.820 --> 01:23:23.620
I know.

1697
01:23:23.740 --> 01:23:28.680
And they have this flashback to their wedding of Jim's brother, you know, reading from Corinthians.

1698
01:23:29.020 --> 01:23:31.000
And, you know, that footage didn't exiSt.

1699
01:23:31.440 --> 01:23:35.380
We had to bring Blake Robbins in and set up the church.

1700
01:23:35.380 --> 01:23:38.300
Just that one corner of the church.

1701
01:23:38.660 --> 01:23:40.100
And he had to do that reading.

1702
01:23:40.100 --> 01:23:41.980
We shot that just for this episode.

1703
01:23:42.180 --> 01:23:45.380
All the other footage was footage that we already had from that episode.

1704
01:23:45.600 --> 01:23:46.920
But this was really beautiful.

1705
01:23:47.240 --> 01:23:49.160
You know, we had a fan question from Marie R.

1706
01:23:49.280 --> 01:23:50.840
in Omaha, Nebraska, who said,

1707
01:23:51.600 --> 01:23:54.900
In the last scene where Jim and Pam hug and then kiss and remember their wedding,

1708
01:23:55.460 --> 01:24:00.420
I noticed that it was in the parking lot where Jim first professed his love for Pam on casino night.

1709
01:24:00.420 --> 01:24:02.800
Was this intentional or just a coincidence?

1710
01:24:03.680 --> 01:24:05.420
Marie, this was intentional.

1711
01:24:06.660 --> 01:24:07.480
It's there.

1712
01:24:07.680 --> 01:24:09.320
It's happening in the same spot.

1713
01:24:09.480 --> 01:24:12.840
This is such a wonderful bookends for their story.

1714
01:24:13.420 --> 01:24:16.740
Kind of the first moment that Jim said, I'm in love with you.

1715
01:24:16.920 --> 01:24:20.020
And then here in the parking lot again to save the marriage.

1716
01:24:20.200 --> 01:24:21.680
Just really beautiful writing.

1717
01:24:22.200 --> 01:24:22.360
Yeah.

1718
01:24:22.960 --> 01:24:24.960
And we talked about this too, Angela.

1719
01:24:24.960 --> 01:24:32.200
You see in that moment the way John Krasinski as Jim swoops down to get to Pam's level for that hug.

1720
01:24:32.420 --> 01:24:35.540
That is a classic John Krasinski hugging move.

1721
01:24:35.840 --> 01:24:37.740
We've talked about this before.

1722
01:24:37.740 --> 01:24:39.540
He gives the best hugs.

1723
01:24:39.820 --> 01:24:41.120
He gives such great hugs.

1724
01:24:41.400 --> 01:24:46.280
He is just like that cozy blanket that makes you feel better.

1725
01:24:46.640 --> 01:24:47.300
I know.

1726
01:24:47.440 --> 01:24:52.940
I just love now that he's a dad and has little girls because I know he hugs them like that.

1727
01:24:52.940 --> 01:24:56.940
You know, I'm like, oh, that's the hug you want.

1728
01:24:57.100 --> 01:24:59.900
That's the hug that makes everything feel like it's going to be okay.

1729
01:25:00.540 --> 01:25:00.900
Yes.

1730
01:25:01.020 --> 01:25:02.400
And it is that kind of hug.

1731
01:25:02.500 --> 01:25:06.980
When he gives you a hug, it is like, oh my gosh, what was that bad day that I was having?

